Loading Mynic File
-----------------------------
- Single Line Comments
- Multi-lined Comments
- All STD datatypes
- typedef   (typedef uint16 header) // Now header is a datatype that can be used
- Datafield settings (uint code {endianness: big, units: "m/s"})
- include other files
- enums
- define    (define HEADER 0) // like enum, but for only one value. Would be useful for branch values & Array sizes
- Default settings for datafields:
    default { // can be place inside of packet to only default with that packer, or global for all packets
        endianness: big,
        units: "m/s"
    }
- bitfields
- unions:
    union multiParse { // Parses bytes as an int then as a float and displays both
        uint32 asInt,
        float32 asFloat
    }
- segment definitions
- Branches to other packets/segment
- bitsX datatype, similar to uint, X can be any positive int -> Prints string of bits
- bytesX datatype, where X is the number of BYTES
- datetime & timespan std types
- Static Arrays:
    {
        uint16 varName[13]; // 13 bytes * 16 bits (2 bytes) = 26 bytes
        bytes2 byteVarName[20]; // 20 groupings of 2 bytes = 40 bytes
    }
- Dynamic arrays:
    {
        uint8 count;
        uint16[count]; // If in same packet
    }

TODO:
-------------------------------
- Add Hex literals (0x00)
- Complex Enums:
    {
        enum uint8 EVENTS {
            E_ONE = 1 { detailSize: 2 },
            E_TWO { detailSize: 1 },
            E_THREE { detailSize: 0 }
        }

        EVENTS event;
        byte details[event.detailSize];
    }
- TO_END keyword, which is used in arrays, loops, etc
{
    bytes[TO_END]; // Collects all of the bytes to the end of the packet -> Note that because there is not a number after "bytes", the array is assumed to be one large chunk of bytes (Same would go for bits[TO_END])
}
- conditional branches (does not actually parse or move the bit index)
    branch bool {
        SEGMENT1 if true;
        SEGMENT2 if false;
        SEGMENT3 defaults;
    }

    branch { // byte is assumed;
        SEGMENT1 if 0x00;
    }
- Repeat fields:
    {
        repeat (10) {
            byte eventHeader
            uint payload
        }

        uint counter
        repeat (counter) { ... }
        
        while (!EOF) { ... }
        while (currentByte != 0x00) { ... }
    }
- Complex Conditional checking in branches:
    branch byte {
        SEGMENT1 if < 0xA3; // Condition logic include (> < >= <= == != %=)
        SEGMENT2 if >= VAR_DEF; // Include operations like + - * / %?
    }

- Checksum (datatype?) -> Evaluates the checksum of the packet and returns true/false in another field acordingly. MUST include all major checksum formats

- Mathematical expressions in values:
    {
        uint16 val {
            expr: bytes * 2
        }
    }
- Binary operators in values? -> May not be needed simply because of the nature of bitfields
- STD math functions
- In file byte processing:
    {
        interpret 656ED7 as PacketName
        ("004FE3", "PacketName")
    }
- File output assigning:
    {
        dump PacketName1, PacketName2 as "JSON" // OR

        dump * as "JSON" { // Each packet gets its own file with the file name being the timestamp
            includeTimestamp: true,
            includeRawBytes: true,
            includePacketName: true,
            destinationFolder: "./folder/path"
        }
    }


- STD Mynic files for popular protocols
    Core Internet: TCP, UDP, IP, ICMP, ARP

    Network Management: SNMP, NetFlow/IPFIX, LLDP

    Secure Networking: TLP, IPsec (ESH/AH)

    Time & Synchronization: NTP, PTP (IEEE 1588)

    Wireless Networking: 802.11 Wifi frame protocols, Bluetooth L2CAP / HCI, Zigbee, LoRaWAN

    Industrial Fieldbus: CAN Bus, CANopen, DeviceNet, PROFIBUS, Modbus RTU, EtherCAT, SERCOS, POWERLINK

    Industrial Ethernet: PROFINET, EtherNet/IP, OPC UA Binary Protocol

    Robotics Framework Protocols: ROS TCPROS/UDPROS, DDS (Data Distribution Service)

    Automotive Systems: CAN (Controller Area Network), LIN (Local Interconnect Network), FlexRay, MOST, Automotive Ethernet, UDS (Unified Diagnostic Services), OBD-II protocol stack

    Aerospace, Satellites, & Rockets
        - Space Communications Standards: CCSDS (Consultative Committee for Space Data Systems), Space Packet Protocol, Telecommand, Telemetry Transfer Frames
        - Satellite Bus: SpaceWire, MIL-STD-1553, ARINC 429, ARINC 664 (AFDX)
        - Ground Communications: SLE (Space Link Extension) protocols, TDM telemetry formats
    
    Embedded/loT Systems: MQTT, CoAP, AMQP, DDS-XRCE, LwM2M

    Low-Power Radios: Thread, Z-Wave, Bluetooth LE

    Data Serialization Protocols: Protocol Buffers (Protobuf), Apache Avro, FlatBuffers, Cap’n Proto, MessagePack, CBOR, BSON

    Finance & Trading: FIX Binary (FAST/SBE), ITCH/OUCH, NASDAQ TotalView ITCH

    Storage & Filesystems: SCSI, iSCSI, NVMe, Fibre Channel, ATA/SATA, NFS (binary RPC), SMB

    Multimedia/Real-Time Streaming: RTP (Real-time Transport Protocol), RTCP, MPEG-TS, WebRTC data channels, QUIC

    Database Wire Protocols: PostgreSQL Wire Protocol, MySQL Protocol, MongoDB Wire Protocol, Redis RESP (partially text but binary safe)

    GPU / High Performance Computing: MPI (Message Passing Interface), RDMA protocols (InfiniBand & RoCE), NVLink

    Telecom / Cellular Networks: SS7, Diameter, GTP (GPRS Tunneling Protocol), SCTP

    Game Networking Protocols: RakNet, ENet, Steam Networking Protocol